**The record stands; I see no supported in-authority step that would move the production decision now.** Keep the running system as the default and make no paid send on the present evidence.

The [Rubin trace](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-6/due-day/RUBIN-TRACE.md>) supports closing this lead for the answer-choice step: the topic itself supplies conflicting windows. The absence of a citation to the regulatory clause does not by itself prove it had no influence, but the trace identifies no sourced correction to that clause.

The invented memory measure remains a **single observed defect**, not a traced general cause. The due-day v2 remains proposed and unadopted; its test was inconclusive. Neither finding supports a production change yet. [D636–D638](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md:980>)

Reopen work on any of [D612’s](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md:956>) conditions: new consequential delivery cases, decidable comparison material, Alex’s marks or decisions, **or a new concrete reversible candidate**. That last route remains available to the council without waiting for Alex.

CONSENSUS: the record stands; no further step is supported on the present evidence.
